      "writtenOn": "2025-11-21T17:19:29Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "OK. But better solution...\n\nI just read all the uses of gsh_strldup, and we can easily re-write to eliminate it:\n\nFirst off, strldup doesn\u0027t limit the resulting string copy to MIN(strlen, l), it just copies l bytes, and NULL terminates.\n\n\nSome callers pass MIN(rc, maxlen) as l, but rc was already limited to maxlen... (some readlink callers).\n\nSome callers are using it to copy a val/len string into utf8strlen, but there the l+1 is actually wrong. utf8string has a {val, len} buffer structure, val is assumed to be NUL terminated, and len is the stringlen, so the buffer val is sized len+1. So putting l+1 into utf8strlen is technically wrong...\n\nI\u0027d have to re-validate if the readlink buffer length is supposed to be the value length or the buffer length (value length + 1 for NUL termination).\n\nWe do need to make sure all these strings are NUL terminated, so strldup may not be right.\n\nLet me make a quick patch to fix all this and eliminate gsh_strldup and then you can rebase your patch on top of mine.",
      "parentUuid": "45496f87_9ef50b61",
      "revId": "6ac461ea252398b77e156ccd3227eb6749a9ad5c",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    }
